  "result": "Perfect! All 185 tests pass, including 10 new voucher tests. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added to `src/errors.js`:**\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: \"An invoice can only have one voucher.\"\n\n**Added to `src/invoices.js`:**\n- `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function that:\n  - Takes a fixed amount in cents off the invoice (after VAT)\n  - Validates the invoice is draft (NOT_DRAFT error)\n  - Prevents multiple vouchers (VOUCHER_EXISTS error)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n  - Returns ok(newInvoice) with invoice.voucher = { code, amount }\n\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to:\n  - Calculate voucher value (0 if no voucher)\n  - Return new field: `voucher`\n  - New total calculation: subtotal - discount + vat - voucher (clamped to 0)\n  - Fixed floating-point precision issue by rounding discount to cents\n\n**Added to `test/invoices.test.js`:**\n- 10 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - invoiceTotals includes voucher field (defaults to 0)\n  - invoiceTotals correctly subtracts voucher from total\n  - applyVoucher adds voucher to draft invoices\n  - applyVoucher fails with NOT_DRAFT for issued invoices\n  - applyVoucher fails with VOUCHER_EXISTS when one already exists\n  - applyVoucher validates amount (non-integer, zero, negative)\n  - applyVoucher preserves invoice properties\n  - invoiceTotals correctly clamps total to 0 when voucher exceeds total\n\n- Updated 10 existing invoiceTotals tests to expect the new `voucher: 0` field\n\nThe implementation allows invoices to have at most one voucher, which reduces a fixed amount from the final invoice total after VAT has been calculated.",
